    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\n[The Cygdb documentation](https://cython.readthedocs.io/en/latest/src/userguide/debugging.html#using-the-debugger) says I should be able to set a breakpoint in Python code and stop the debugger there, but it doesn't work. The breakpoint appears to be there, but the debugger doesn't stop.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n[Here's a repository with demonstration code](https://github.com/clayote/cygdb-bug-demo). When you've checked it out and changed directory into it, run: \n```shell\npython setup.py build_ext --inplace\ncygdb --build-dir . -- --args python runthis.py\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nThe debugger, following the ``.cygdbinit`` commands, should stop at the first line of the ``main()`` function in ``runthis.py``\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.6\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0a2.dev0\n\n### Additional context\n\nI used a virtualenv with a Python I built myself, using the `--with-pydebug` configuration option. I also built gdb 17.2 `--with-python`.",
